{title: 327 - I'd Rather Have Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #327 • ID RATHER HAVE JESUS • 11.11.11.10}
{lyricist: Rhea F. Miller}
{composer: George Beverly Shea}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 327}
{meta: tune ID RATHER HAVE JESUS}
{meta: meter 11.11.11.10}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]I'd rather have Jesus than [Am]silver [F]or [C]gold;
[C]I'd rather be His than have riches untold;
[G7/D]I'd [C]rather have Jesus than houses or [Am]land;
[F]I'd rather [C]be led by His nailpierced hand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[C/E]Than to [F]be the [C/G]king [G7]of a [C]vast domain [G7/D]or [C]be held [G7]in sin's dread [Am]sway!
[F]I'd rather [C]have Jesus than anything this [G7]world affords today.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]I'd rather have Jesus than [Am]men's [F]applause;
[C]I'd rather be faithful to His dear cause;
[G7/D]I'd [C]rather have Jesus than world-wide fame;
[F]I'd rather [C]be true to His holy name:
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]He's fairer than lilies of [Am]rarest [F]bloom;
[C]He's sweeter than honey from out the comb;
[G7/D]He's [C]all [G]that [C]my hungering spirit needs [Am]-
[F]I'd rather [C]have Jesus and let Him lead:
{end_of_verse}
